<p>My company is pretty paranoid about leaking IP to the frontier labs through prompts, so we've all been diligent about disabling data sharing in Codex/Claude Code/etc. But yesterday my coworkers and I noticed that the setting had been silently reenabled in Codex. None of us knowingly opted back in.<p>You can check your settings here: https://chatgpt.com/settings/data-controls. Look for "Improve the model for everyone".<p>Curious if this is an isolated issue or something more widespread.<p>EDIT: looks like this has been noted before https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49643556<p>EDIT: apparently you can also turn off data sharing here: https://privacy.openai.com/policies?modal=take-control</p>
